    "Content delivery networks cache content on servers geographically closer to users to cut delay; streaming companies use them to deliver video; a miss goes back to the origin server: https://aws.amazon.com/what-is/cdn/ ; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Content_delivery_network",
    "Video is broken into short segments, typically 2-6 seconds each (one platform's spec: target 6 seconds): https://www.mux.com/articles/adaptive-bitrate-streaming-guide ; https://bitmovin.com/blog/mpeg-dash-hls-segment-length/ ; https://developer.apple.com/documentation/http-live-streaming/hls-authoring-specification-for-apple-devices",
    "Each segment is encoded at multiple bitrates/resolutions; the player decides which version to request next from its bandwidth estimate, switching up or down between segments: https://www.mux.com/articles/adaptive-bitrate-streaming-guide ; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adaptive_bitrate_streaming ; https://bitmovin.com/blog/mpeg-dash-hls-segment-length/",
